s money and incumbency reframe the race among South Texas Hispanic voters in the final weeks.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Monica De La Cruz (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Texas's 15th District in South Texas leans Republican by about seven points, but Monica De La Cruz's defense of the seat has become one of the cycle's most competitive House races. Democrat Bobby Pulido, a well-known Tejano singer, has run a heavily funded campaign built on crossover outreach to Hispanic voters, and national Democrats view the district as one of their best pickup opportunities.\n\nRecent polling shows Pulido narrowly to clearly ahead, with the newest survey giving him a double-digit lead, and prediction markets price his chances around four in five. Still, most professional raters call the race a tossup or a slight Republican edge, citing the district's partisan lean and the incumbent's financial advantage. All told, the race points to a narrow Democratic edge with meaningful uncertainty remaining.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4454, "margin": -0.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6234, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6548, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6308, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5679, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6942, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6077, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6479, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7065, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6601, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6541, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6766, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}]}